Changes in version 0.99.15 (2026-07-18)
-----------------------------------------

Algorithm Correctness

* Added `target_priority` parameter (default `"promoter_then_distance"`) to
  `annotate_peaks_and_loops()`.  The policy applies only within primary target
  links (default `path_length <= 1`); longer paths are reported separately as
  `Expanded_Target_Genes` and do not compete for `Assigned_Target_Genes`.
  `promoter_then_distance` gives promoter-linked evidence priority over
  gene-body links within the primary-link scope; `distance_then_role` restores
  the legacy path-length-dominant behaviour.  This parameter is propagated
  through expression refinement and chromatin refinement.  Tied genes with the
  same optimal priority are preserved (semicolon-delimited).
* Reordered chromatin reclassification rules to fix three blocking issues:
  (1) enhancer BED is now truly highest priority; (2) eP/eG dual_like anchors
  correctly resolve via bigWig ratio (me1_dominant → dual, unresolved → keep,
  not_me1_dominant → P); (3) eP/eG with H3K4me3+ but without H3K4me1+
  (promoter_like) revert to P.  Bivalent H3K4me3+/H3K27me3+ anchors are
  resolved by these rules (H3K4me3 defines promoter identity), not by the
  generic conflicting_marks clause.
* Triple-positive anchors (H3K4me1+/H3K4me3+/H3K27me3+) are now classified
  as conflicting_marks and retain their previous eP/eG type. Peak
  co-occurrence from bulk ChIP alone is not considered sufficient evidence
  for restoration to a functional promoter state.
* Removed duplicate E/G dual-positive rules that became unreachable after
  reordering.
* Fixed duplicate `mutate()` columns (role_rank, path_rank) that caused
  a dplyr error in `.aggregate_strict_targets()`.
* Fixed `up_meta_params` scope bug in expression refinement target finalizer.

Documentation

* Fixed BED-only mode documentation to accurately describe dual-positive anchor
  retention (H3K4me1+/H3K4me3+ anchors keep eP/eG type pending bigWig resolution).
* Removed misleading measured_set reference from reclassify_by_expression documentation.
* Corrected vignette BED-only mode descriptions for chromatin reclassification rules.
* Fixed vignette gsea_nSample default (NULL, not 99999) to match profile_target_genes().
* Fixed validate_epeG_by_chromatin() and chromatin-refine examples in vignette.
* Fixed README "within 10% of max" → "at least 10% of the group maximum" for
  co_dominance_ratio description.
* Changed "ENCODE criteria" → "ENCODE-inspired criteria" in report template (4 occurrences).

Testing & Engineering

* Removed file-level skip_on_bioc() from 3 core regression test files
  (test-regression.R, test-synthetic-invariants.R, test-review-fixes.R)
  so critical invariants run on Bioconductor builders.
* Updated 3 recompute_targets = FALSE tests to expect preserved upstream
  target tables (not NULL), matching the unified finalizer behavior.
* Added globalVariables() declarations for 30+ dplyr/data.table NSE symbols
  in annotation.R and data_processing.R, resolving R CMD check NOTES.
* Fixed roxygen block separation for .passes_expression_threshold().

Changes in version 0.99.14 (2026-06-21)
-----------------------------------------

Algorithm & Correctness

* Fixed case-sensitive gene name matching: clean_anchor() and resolve_gene_conflicts()
  now use toupper() on both sides, preventing silent P→eP misclassification when
  expression matrix row names differ in case from OrgDb SYMBOLs.
* Added biotype_order parameter to annotate_peaks_and_loops() and resolve_gene_conflicts(),
  allowing users to customise biotype priority order (e.g., prioritise lncRNAs).
* Case-insensitive diagnostic warning in expression-refinement overlap check.

Chromatin Refinement Visualizations

* Added Chromatin_Sankey: anchor-type flow diagram showing reclassification direction
  (unchanged = green, reclassified = amber).
* Added Chromatin_MarkHeatmap: aggregated ComplexHeatmap showing mark enrichment %
  per reclassification group, with N count bar annotation.
* Chromatin_Dumbbell: updated to grey-green academic palette (Original = #999999,
  Refined = #2D5A3D) for consistency with Expression Refinement module.

Documentation

* Added @seealso cross-references between annotate_peaks_and_loops(),
  refine_loop_anchors_by_expression(), refine_loop_anchors_by_chromatin(),
  and profile_target_genes().
* Updated roxygen for .build_chromatin_mark_heatmap() to match actual implementation.

Changes in version 0.99.9 (2026-05-09)
-----------------------------------------

Reviewer Response (Bisaloo, Bioconductor)

* Added package-level man page and runnable examples for all exported functions.
* Replaced sapply() with vapply(); removed <<- operator; eliminated dead code.
* Unified 0-based BED/BEDPE import and 1-based internal coordinate handling.
* Fixed GO enrichment table rendering (list-of-dataframes merge).
* Fixed expression matrix gene-name loss with single-sample-column input.
* Fixed OrgDb object handling via getFromNamespace() instead of get().
* Added whitelist-overlap cross-validation warning in expression refinement.
* Added empty-input guards for ChIPseeker::annotatePeak() and prepare_track_data().
* Replaced deprecated ggplot2 size aesthetic with linewidth.
* Improved test coverage to 84.70% with 29 dedicated regression tests.
* Updated default colour palettes to colourblind-friendly schemes (Set2, Paired, PuOr, viridis).
* looplook_report() template: enhanced metric cards, Sankey via saveWidget+iframe, aligned tables.
* Vignette: expanded comparison table, reproducibility note, BiocManager install placeholder.
* DESCRIPTION: Title case, non-package-name Description start, removed recursive SystemRequirements, expanded Suggests.
* Precomputed results now accepted as in-memory list or file path; bedpe_file optional.

Changes in version 0.99.0 (2026-03-02)
-----------------------------------------
* Comprehensive refactoring for Bioconductor submission, including Expression-Aware modules and enhanced vignettes.